{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities","id":1481892,"title":"Constructing and Unravelling Cover Identities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-24T19:39:18-07:00","id":1481892,"title":"Constructing and Unravelling Cover Identities","content":"How would the Technocracy build a &quot;Jacket&quot; for an under cover agent, as a Tradition Mage, both in the mundane and magical senses?<br /> <br /> It seems like it would be fairly easy for players to unravel the fabricated identity. How can this be made difficult and that difficulty make sense, rules wise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T05:39:05-07:00","id":1481913,"title":"","content":"It depends on the amount of resources the Technocracy is investing, or in game terms the amount of success we assume they have in building the jacket. Mind sphere would make the agent believe their own cover story, and that level of brain washing does appear in fiction. Spirit could be used to mask the aura. Backgrounds provide, well, background, such as an apparent history, money, contacts and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit; Maybe the real question is how hard is it supposed to be for the PCs to crack through the cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 05-25-2022, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T06:31:28-07:00","id":1481916,"title":"","content":"Part of it is that you probably want your \u201cmage\u201d performing some sort of magick other than Enlightened Science. In my games, this is where the SPD comes in: not in the sense of \u201cWyrm-Tainted agents\u201d, but in the sense of \u201cagents who are trained in the practice of \u2018fringe science\u2019\u201d. As a guideline, I figure that SPD agents are among the rare few among the Technocracy who can (and usually do) acquire the \u201cScientific Mystic\u201d Merit \u2014 though in their case, it's not so much that they \u201cunderstand the science behind the magic\u201d as it is that they understand the magic well enough to \u201cfake it\u201d using science. That, combined with a willingness of these agents to actually make in some discredited science (the sort of stuff that the Society of Ether is infamous for), and you have a Technocratic agent who can pass herself off as a Hermetic, Chorister, Akashayana, or any other Tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T09:31:17-07:00","id":1481930,"title":"","content":"You would need to think how to make the Chantry established memebers accept the mage. Some way to make the troupe accept what's by all means a very important and influential character inside their circle.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> <br /> The best way I can think of it's to &quot;replace&quot; one of the mages. Make an npc mage of the chantry go visit &quot;room 101&quot; in his free time, and quickly dump his identity on the cover agent. Mind 4 should have you covered. Of course you want to implant fake memories and all that. If only as a Mind illusion (using Mind 2) to prevent mind reading mages to detect your agent's affiliation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can fake a backstory within the traditions and/or some sort of recommendation to get accepted as a newcomer. But that's risky, because the Chantry can and should doublecheck. That cover ain't likely to last long w/o a very extensive net.<br /> <br /> If the Chantry it's recruiting new members, one could masquerade as a potential candidate (like, a talented Orphan or a newly Awakened). Problem is, in hierarchical Traditions being &quot;new&quot; may involve going to the Horizon Chantry and passing trough very trough tests. May even be sent to another Chantry, if some superior likes the mage, or just feels like screwing with the mages <hr /><br /> As said by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> , one problem of infiltrating &quot;as a mage&quot; (instead of, say, as an Acolite) it's that you will be expected to do the magick of your Tradition. Or at least fake it well enough.<br /> <br /> Technomancers would be the easier route - Like, most can't tell the difference between a VA and a Technocrat anyway, just by changing the surface, using some of that (very much mandatory) Tradition Lore, any compter saavy NWO agent could pass as one.<br /> <br /> As a more extreme idea: &quot;room 101&quot; can force a change of Paradigm on a mage to make a Traditionalist into a Technocrat. That being the case, I imagine it could similarly (and more easily, because it would be voluntary) adjust an agent's Paradigm to a more mystic mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-25-2022, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T20:58:14-07:00","id":1481979,"title":"","content":"One of my players has both Time and Correspondence above 2. Normally, that makes looking at someone's history fairly easy. Is there any way to make it stand up under such scrutiny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T10:35:49-07:00","id":1482007,"title":"","content":"You can block such perceptions, but then it would be obvious that the character it's hidding something because of the nature of such blockades...<br /> <br /> One of the advantages of replacing someone it's that these type of invasive scans aren't normal to do on people you know.<br /> But you could, perhaps,<b> fake a whole chantry?</b><br /> <br /> With actors and technomacy, some of that &quot;hollywood magic&quot; - for your fake mage to have lived in for a time. That way, when the character scans the near past, he sees the chantry where your mage supposedly comes from. Who knows?, if this has been going for a while, it may even be an official chantry.<br /> <br /> The risk it's that you don't know how far into the past mages would look. But, within reason, I imagine not a whole lot. Seers wouldn't want to relive your entire life, just some events and moments. A couple months, perhaps with visits covering special dates (the moment you got in or sent out?, a fake &quot;graduation&quot; of sorts?. Last Christmass?, I mean, you could actually have a blockade on some of those and just say it's private.). It could be useful to think about the kind of &quot;questions&quot; such a perception would want answered (you can always use ST prerogative to determine it was &quot;covered&quot;, post facto, but it could be interesting if some &quot;questions&quot; could actually unravel the ruse - instead of just &quot;it works because I say so&quot;. IDK).<br /> <br /> All in all, it has the potential of being fun, I think. When your players discover the ruse, it may lead to an organized attack on the &quot;hollywood chantry&quot; Construct. Now, that I would want to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />Using magick.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, albeit this is a bit of a stretch, verging on house rule territory (if not going rigth in) - and thus may be unfair if you haven't brough this up as a posibility for magick - you could craft a Time/Corr block in such a way that, instead of just blocking the attempt, it makes an illusion. The principle would be similar to the Mind <b>2</b>version of the mind shield in revised, &quot;No Mind&quot;, that makes the mind reader see as if the mind was empty, instead of just not being able to enter. It stands to reason, in my opinion, that Mind 3 would be able to place complex ilussions such as fake toughts. And maybe, combined with Time/Corr 2 (that would have to be 3, at least on the Corr side) blockades, to replace what the seer would see with a fake vision.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, using Time triggers, a Prime-based cybernetics, or both, you could have this as a magical <i>attack </i>on the scanning mage's mind. A Procedure that <i>reacts</i> to such a scan with an illusion that replaces what's seen. More complex, arguably easier to detect, but could be more fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-26-2022, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T12:09:41-07:00","id":1482016,"title":"","content":"Everett Volumes (alternate histories) are a thing in Mage. Identify an Everett Volume where your spy <i>actually was</i> a mage; then arrange an Adjustment that redirects any inquiries into your past so that they delve into that Everett Volume. Maybe treat it as a Data/Time Adjustment: Data to intercept any attempts to connect to the mole, and Time to redirect into the Everett Volume. This could even be an NWO Adjustment where the Instruments involved are government records; the only \u201chandwavery\u201d involved here is how changes to those records (the Instrument used in this particular Adjustment) results in Magickal scrying into your mole's past being redirected into a fictional timeline. <br /> <br /> But frankly, that's part of the NWO's \u201cEverything is Data\u201d Paradigm \u2014 or is it their \u201cBelief Shapes Reality\u201d Paradigm? In particular, it's very much in keeping with the very NWOish idea that those who can define the past can shape the future. So they use this Adjustment to define the past \u2014 if not literally, then close enough for government work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:21:01-07:00","id":1482163,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities?p=1481913#post1481913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the amount of resources the Technocracy is investing, or in game terms the amount of success we assume they have in building the jacket. Mind sphere would make the agent believe their own cover story, and that level of brain washing does appear in fiction. Spirit could be used to mask the aura. Backgrounds provide, well, background, such as an apparent history, money, contacts and so on.<br /> <br /> Edit; Maybe the real question is how hard is it supposed to be for the PCs to crack through the cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my WoD, the Void Engineers aren't even teaching Dimensional Science to the NWO to fight Pentex, because I scrapped Pentex. Earthly Technomancers are Spirit-blind. On the flip side, Primal Utility remains a Syndicate secret. I think Prime and Mind together are good for masking Auras, Good idea.<br /> <br /> One of the ways I have decided to make it challenging is to include surface details about the spy in a large info-dump that is very layered. Everything happens at once and they have to think fast. They might have doubts about her, but they are juggling a lot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities?p=1481916#post1481916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of it is that you probably want your \u201cmage\u201d performing some sort of magick other than Enlightened Science. In my games, this is where the SPD comes in: not in the sense of \u201cWyrm-Tainted agents\u201d, but in the sense of \u201cagents who are trained in the practice of \u2018fringe science\u2019\u201d. As a guideline, I figure that SPD agents are among the rare few among the Technocracy who can (and usually do) acquire the \u201cScientific Mystic\u201d Merit \u2014 though in their case, it's not so much that they \u201cunderstand the science behind the magic\u201d as it is that they understand the magic well enough to \u201cfake it\u201d using science. That, combined with a willingness of these agents to actually make in some discredited science (the sort of stuff that the Society of Ether is infamous for), and you have a Technocratic agent who can pass herself off as a Hermetic, Chorister, Akashayana, or any other Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Syndicate's Special Security Information Division. I actually have a plot involving them that would make for a good post, sometime. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities?p=1481930#post1481930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would need to think how to make the Chantry established memebers accept the mage. Some way to make the troupe accept what's by all means a very important and influential character inside their circle.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<br /> <br /> The best way I can think of it's to &quot;replace&quot; one of the mages. Make an npc mage of the chantry go visit &quot;room 101&quot; in his free time, and quickly dump his identity on the cover agent. Mind 4 should have you covered. Of course you want to implant fake memories and all that. If only as a Mind illusion (using Mind 2) to prevent mind reading mages to detect your agent's affiliation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can fake a backstory within the traditions and/or some sort of recommendation to get accepted as a newcomer. But that's risky, because the Chantry can and should doublecheck. That cover ain't likely to last long w/o a very extensive net.<br /> <br /> If the Chantry it's recruiting new members, one could masquerade as a potential candidate (like, a talented Orphan or a newly Awakened). Problem is, in hierarchical Traditions being &quot;new&quot; may involve going to the Horizon Chantry and passing trough very trough tests. May even be sent to another Chantry, if some superior likes the mage, or just feels like screwing with the mages <hr /><br /> As said by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> , one problem of infiltrating &quot;as a mage&quot; (instead of, say, as an Acolite) it's that you will be expected to do the magick of your Tradition. Or at least fake it well enough.<br /> <br /> Technomancers would be the easier route - Like, most can't tell the difference between a VA and a Technocrat anyway, just by changing the surface, using some of that (very much mandatory) Tradition Lore, any compter saavy NWO agent could pass as one.<br /> <br /> As a more extreme idea: &quot;room 101&quot; can force a change of Paradigm on a mage to make a Traditionalist into a Technocrat. That being the case, I imagine it could similarly (and more easily, because it would be voluntary) adjust an agent's Paradigm to a more mystic mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Total Manchurian Candidate.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities?p=1482007#post1482007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can block such perceptions, but then it would be obvious that the character it's hidding something because of the nature of such blockades...<br /> <br /> One of the advantages of replacing someone it's that these type of invasive scans aren't normal to do on people you know.<br /> But you could, perhaps,<b> fake a whole chantry?</b><br /> <br /> With actors and technomacy, some of that &quot;hollywood magic&quot; - for your fake mage to have lived in for a time. That way, when the character scans the near past, he sees the chantry where your mage supposedly comes from. Who knows?, if this has been going for a while, it may even be an official chantry.<br /> <br /> The risk it's that you don't know how far into the past mages would look. But, within reason, I imagine not a whole lot. Seers wouldn't want to relive your entire life, just some events and moments. A couple months, perhaps with visits covering special dates (the moment you got in or sent out?, a fake &quot;graduation&quot; of sorts?. Last Christmass?, I mean, you could actually have a blockade on some of those and just say it's private.). It could be useful to think about the kind of &quot;questions&quot; such a perception would want answered (you can always use ST prerogative to determine it was &quot;covered&quot;, post facto, but it could be interesting if some &quot;questions&quot; could actually unravel the ruse - instead of just &quot;it works because I say so&quot;. IDK).<br /> <br /> All in all, it has the potential of being fun, I think. When your players discover the ruse, it may lead to an organized attack on the &quot;hollywood chantry&quot; Construct. Now, that I would want to see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr />Using magick.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, albeit this is a bit of a stretch, verging on house rule territory (if not going rigth in) - and thus may be unfair if you haven't brough this up as a posibility for magick - you could craft a Time/Corr block in such a way that, instead of just blocking the attempt, it makes an illusion. The principle would be similar to the Mind <b>2</b>version of the mind shield in revised, &quot;No Mind&quot;, that makes the mind reader see as if the mind was empty, instead of just not being able to enter. It stands to reason, in my opinion, that Mind 3 would be able to place complex ilussions such as fake toughts. And maybe, combined with Time/Corr 2 (that would have to be 3, at least on the Corr side) blockades, to replace what the seer would see with a fake vision.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, using Time triggers, a Prime-based cybernetics, or both, you could have this as a magical <i>attack </i>on the scanning mage's mind. A Procedure that <i>reacts</i> to such a scan with an illusion that replaces what's seen. More complex, arguably easier to detect, but could be more fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's definitely an imposter. During the interrogation of the now dead Mage, the imposter made a genuine offer to take care of any last wishes. She continues to fulfill the request, system-wise, having the Sworn Obligation Flaw. The player scrying might see glimpses of the interrogation, but be confused about who is saying what, since this is the point where one takes on the memories of the other, Room 101 style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481892-constructing-and-unravelling-cover-identities?p=1482016#post1482016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everett Volumes (alternate histories) are a thing in Mage. Identify an Everett Volume where your spy <i>actually was</i> a mage; then arrange an Adjustment that redirects any inquiries into your past so that they delve into that Everett Volume. Maybe treat it as a Data/Time Adjustment: Data to intercept any attempts to connect to the mole, and Time to redirect into the Everett Volume. This could even be an NWO Adjustment where the Instruments involved are government records; the only \u201chandwavery\u201d involved here is how changes to those records (the Instrument used in this particular Adjustment) results in Magickal scrying into your mole's past being redirected into a fictional timeline.<br /> <br /> But frankly, that's part of the NWO's \u201cEverything is Data\u201d Paradigm \u2014 or is it their \u201cBelief Shapes Reality\u201d Paradigm? In particular, it's very much in keeping with the very NWOish idea that those who can define the past can shape the future. So they use this Adjustment to define the past \u2014 if not literally, then close enough for government work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everett Volume redirection solves the last detail and players get to learn the metaphysical significance of a birth certificate. <br /> <br /> Thanks, everyone<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T10:47:42-07:00","id":1482174,"title":"","content":"My only concern is that by making non-VE Technocrats Spirit-blind, you're opening them up to borderline-trivial exploits. No self-respecting Chantry wouldn't have a Spirit mage who has the local spirits keeping watch on the doings of the local Construct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T13:27:32-07:00","id":1482189,"title":"","content":"The Spacemen keep a careful watch with satellites or, better yet, the satellites are Wonders constructed for use by Construct bosses. Research and Execution.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited